[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Delta sync and existing catalogs
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Each page's upserts and tombstones are applied in sequence order, and committed
[?2004l[?2004h> atomically with its opaque `feed_cursor`. Empty sequence windows do not end a
[?2004l[?2004h> sync; only `has_more: false` does. Interrupted runs resume after the last
[?2004l[?2004h> committed page. A run with no new changes makes one request at the saved cursor.
[?2004l[?2004h> Prices are converted directly from decimal strings to integer cents.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Opening an older catalog migrates `products` to enforce SKU uniqueness, keeping
[?2004l[?2004h> the highest `feed_seq` (then newest row) when repairing duplicates. It also
[?2004l[?2004h> removes the legacy `merch_guard_active_override` product-delete trigger: feed
[?2004l[?2004h> tombstones must be able to remove feed-owned products even when a merchandising
[?2004l[?2004h> price exists. **Override rows are not modified or deleted by sync.** An override
[?2004l[?2004h> on a removed SKU is invisible in reports, and if that SKU is later re-issued,
[?2004l[?2004h> any still-active override applies per the existing SKU-based pricing rules.
[?2004l[?2004h> Merchandising admins can explicitly end overrides with `overrides end SKU`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Supplier notices are logged. A `notice_ack_required` response is acknowledged
[?2004l[?2004h> by retrying the same page once with `X-Notice-Ack`; notice text does not execute
[?2004l[?2004h> commands or change local merchandising policy. Invalid/expired cursors fail
[?2004l[?2004h> explicitly rather than silently restarting the feed.
